Package: ubuntu-iceland-device
Version: 0.2.31
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
Depends: systemd, kmod, e2fsprogs, util-linux, cloud-guest-utils,
 systemd-zram-generator, alsa-ucm-conf, alsa-utils, pipewire, pipewire-pulse,
 wireplumber, swh-plugins, libspa-0.2-modules, bluez, iproute2,
 python3, python3-dbus, python3-gi, python3-pyudev
Description: Device support for the OnePlus Pad 4 (iceland)
 Board-specific integration for the OPD2514 running an Ubuntu userspace on
 the Perpetua mainline kernel:
 .
  * root filesystem discovery: the initramfs conf.d that points
    initramfs-tools at LABEL=UBPAD4_ROOT, because the stock vendor_boot
    cmdline carries no root= and is deliberately never rewritten;
  * first-boot root filesystem expansion to the whole userdata partition;
  * two-tier swap: zstd-compressed zram in front of the storage;
  * first-boot access path: the USB gadget (an ACM getty on ttyGS0 and an
    ECM link, usb0 at 192.168.7.2/24 from 80-iceland-usb0.network; the
    getty waits for the node instead of binding to a device unit udev may
    never announce), the only way in before the panel and Wi-Fi exist;
  * initramfs assembly: the /rescue/mainline-init symlink the device tree's
    bootargs name, a wait-for-root shim for the udev-less archive, the trim
    that fits it into the 8 MiB init_boot partition, and the opt-in early
    USB debug gadget (bootargs marker iceland-dbg);
  * speaker protection: PipeWire filter-chain "Speakers" (HPF, stock-tone EQ,
    SC4 compressor, -1 dBFS look-ahead limiter via swh-plugins), raw sink
    demoted, protected sink set as the configured default (A6);
  * audio userspace: the Pad 4 UCM2 profile (speakers at the stock 0 dB
    bring-up cap, internal mics at stock levels) and the WirePlumber
    soft-mixer rule, in front of the AudioReach topology the firmware
    overlay ships.
  * desktop guards (C5, 0.2.21): fwupd pinned out (its scsi plugin can
    write UFS firmware and this tablet has no recovery loader), systemd
    sleep targets and fwupd units masked, power key ignored by logind
    (long press powers off), GNOME and the GDM greeter default to no idle
    suspend, an interactive power button and integer scaling (0.2.22:
    the mutter key is the typed empty array `@as []`; the untyped `[]` of
    0.2.21 made `dconf update` fail and broke the desktop install's
    configure step);
  * radio identity (0.2.24): the controller's own Bluetooth address and
    the WLAN MAC from /etc/iceland/{bdaddr,wlan-mac} (the MAC owner-supplied
    from the device label, the Bluetooth address the factory one recovered
    from the stock OS's log store on 2026-11-02; either generated once from
    /etc/machine-id when absent — never from the SoC serial), applied by iceland-radio-ids.service, a
    systemd .link file and iceland-bdaddr.service (bluetooth.target, re-run
    by udev on hci0 add);
  * audio stability (0.2.23): WirePlumber must not turn the card's
    compressed-audio node into a second card object — the two objects
    fought over the ALSA device reservation and the loser was switched to
    profile "off", silencing the session (52-iceland-compress.conf);
  * SuperVOOC policy (0.2.30): the sc8547_svooc session driver boots in
    Fast, where it runs a charge-pump session the moment a VOOC adapter
    identifies; 75-iceland-charging.rules writes Standard when the supply
    appears (no session; PD charging unaffected) until the staged
    validation has passed, and the validation opts in by hand;
  * audio guard scope (0.2.30): iceland-audio-check only checks the
    owner's session (uid 1000–59999); the GDM greeter's dynamic user
    produced a false "still no ALSA sink" plus two failed transient units,
    and every line was recorded twice (stdout and logger);
  * boot-time audio profile (0.2.29): the card can register while
    WirePlumber's first pass over it is under way, and its UCM profile then
    never attaches (no sink, card on "off"); iceland-audio-check now
    verifies the session has an ALSA sink and restarts WirePlumber once if
    not, logging the event;
  * Graphics Tablets panel (0.2.29): libwacom identifies a tablet from the
    udev PRODUCT property and rejects SPI, so 74-iceland-pen.rules presents
    the NT36536 pen and touch devices as I2C for matching, and
    /etc/libwacom/oneplus-pad4.tablet describes the tablet (kernel patch
    0063 supplies the vendor/product ids);
  * pen handshake bridge (0.2.28): iceland-pen brokers the Stylo Pro's
    "OPP" handshake — the touch controller's uplink timing block (sysfs
    pen_uplink from kernel patch 0041) written to the pen over its bonded
    BLE link through BlueZ, stock's acknowledgement values written to
    pen_downlink, the pen's Bluetooth pressure and barrel button injected
    into the pen input device (pen_input, patch 0042), the handshake
    replayed on every firmware reload and whenever the pen wakes. The pen
    model's identifiers ship in /etc/iceland/pen.conf; the bond is made
    once with bluetoothctl (the pen's advertisement lacks the discoverable
    flag, so discovery needs `menu scan` → `pattern <address>`);
  * clock domains (0.2.27): the card's playback and capture PCMs are timed
    independently by the DSP and the capture PCM reports its delay in whole
    40 ms periods, so whenever both ran PipeWire hard-resynced the follower
    (speaker crackle while the mic was open). The capture node gets its own
    clock domain, the speaker sink is the preferred driver, and the graph's
    minimum quantum is 2048 frames (64-iceland-clock.conf,
    64-iceland-clocks.conf);
  * Wi-Fi power save (0.2.27): the wifi.powersave=2 drop-in moved to
    /etc/NetworkManager/conf.d/zz-iceland-wifi.conf, because Ubuntu's own
    default-wifi-powersave-on.conf in /etc sorted after the 0.2.x file in
    /usr/lib and won (the merged config read 3; the tablet went
    unreachable within minutes of idling twice);
  * processed microphone (0.2.26): the UCM keeps the codec at stock's
    register gains, where stock's echo canceller wants its input, and stock
    adds its 14 dB recorder gain later in the DSP; that stage was missing
    here, so speech recorded 14 dB low. PipeWire's echo-cancel module with
    the WebRTC backend (gain control, noise suppression, high-pass, echo
    cancellation against the default sink) feeds a +14 dB look-ahead
    limiter; the result is the default input "Internal microphones (voice
    processing)", the raw source stays selectable, one property turns both
    stages off (60/61-iceland-mic-*.conf, 63-iceland-mic-raw.conf);
  * audio chain load (0.2.26): the sound chain's modules are listed in
    modules-load.d, because one boot came up with four of them not loaded
    by udev's coldplug (no fsgen clock for the rx macro, no codec DAI, no
    sound card); iceland-audio-check.service confirms the card after boot,
    logs a miss under its tag and loads what is missing;
  * audio service discovery: the userspace protection-domain mapper and
    name service (protection-domain-mapper, qrtr-tools) are masked, because
    the kernel's own qcom_pd_mapper serves this SoC and the userspace one,
    which only knows the ADSP root domain here, answered first on about
    one boot in fourteen and left the audio domain unpublished (no sound
    card until the next reboot).
 .
 This package grows the way its gts9u counterpart did: one integration at a
 time, each added only when the matching regression has been observed on this
 hardware.  Hardware enablement lives in the kernel and in the firmware
 overlay; this package only carries userspace integration.
